  "response_text": "__io_putchar acts as a wrapper function that is called by the printf function to output individual characters to the UART or console. Since the printf function is part of the stdio library, which is designed for general-purpose systems, a wrapper like __io_putchar is necessary to bridge the gap between the library and the hardware-specific input/output channel.\\n",
